    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0938bc24_b7b115fd",
        "filename": "java/droidstubs.go",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 401,
      "author": {
        "id": 1061164
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-06-29T13:27:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I will update the comment, but glad you asked 😊\n\nNeither system nor module-lib apis exist since API level 1. SystemApis for apps are 21+ concept, and modulelibs are even later.\n\nThe order is important even outside of the mainline context, as some relevant files/stubs for older releases are in a different place.\n\nAt runtime metalava attempts to find the stubs for a certain release X by going through all the patterns we pass to it. So, if we are building framework-doc-system-stubs for example, it will use system stubs for 21+, and public stubs for 20-.\n\nThis only really matters if we care about older releases, e.g. 1p apps with mintargetsdk\u003d19. If not, metalava accepts --first-version arg to say that we only care about 29+ for example.",
      "parentUuid": "e8d4794b_67770673",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 400,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 401,
        "endChar": 70
      },
      "revId": "9b6246e5049758c58202a08ffa5307b7ba932301",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
